@startuml
title Desmoche - Fase 5: autoridad y vistas privadas
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
package "Proceso host (peer 1)" {
  [Presentacion host] as HUI
  [NetworkManager\nENet servidor] as HN
  [ServerSession\nregistro peer -> jugador] as S
  [GameManager\nmaquina de estados] as G
  [GameState\nmanos y mazo privados] as GS
  [RulesValidator] as R
}
package "Proceso cliente" {
  [Presentacion cliente] as CUI
  [NetworkManager\nENet cliente] as CN
  [SnapshotDto\nmano propia + estado publico] as V
}
HUI --> HN : Submit
HN --> S : misma validacion para host
CN --> HN : Hello / RequestAction
HN --> CN : Admission / ReceiveView / ActionReply\nRpcId destinatario
S --> G : accion del jugador vinculado al peer
G --> GS
G --> R
S --> HN : vista individual
CN --> V
V --> CUI
CUI --> CN : Submit
note bottom of GS
Nunca serializar GameState ni Player.
El orden del mazo y las manos ajenas
no salen del servidor durante la partida.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title Una solicitud remota
actor Jugador
participant "Cliente NetworkManager" as C
participant "Host NetworkManager" as N
participant ServerSession as S
participant GameManager as G
Jugador -> C : Submit(accion, datos)
C -> N : RequestAction(JSON)
N -> N : capturar GetRemoteSenderId()
N -> S : Receive(peer, JSON, reloj)
S -> S : identidad, cuota, estructura,\nsesion, solicitud, ventana
S -> G : validar y aplicar accion
G --> S : resultado y estado
S -> G : ResolveClaims si todos respondieron
S --> N : ReplyDto
N -> S : ViewFor(cada peer)
S --> N : snapshot individual
N -> C : ReceiveView(vista privada)
N -> C : ActionReply(resultado)
C -> Jugador : actualizar presentacion
@enduml
